    "done_when": "The review of a-stopped-run-ends-its-supervisor (96) found that in tests/test_a_stopped_run_ends_its_supervisor.py the line 'assert elapsed < WORKER_SLEEP_SECONDS' can never fail. The _wait_until before it returns only once the supervisor's pid is gone within CEILING_SECONDS (90 s), which is below WORKER_SLEEP_SECONDS (120 s), so the line adds no bound, while its comment presents it as the separate discriminator. The node replaces it with a bound that can fail. One option is an elapsed bound derived from STOP_GRACE_SECONDS plus the supervisor poll interval and the SIGKILL escalation, with a stated load margin, that stays below CEILING_SECONDS. The other is to delete the line and rewrite the comment to name what discriminates: the ceiling and the worker-ignored-the-stop-grace-signal sender reason. The node names its choice and its reason in the commit body. The file passes; the declared negative control is executed and logged.",
